# Capture user proposals as vault notes

When the user suggests a product/engine change, reports a bug, or says "хочу / давай / надо / баг / сломалось" as a durable idea — **create a markdown note in `vault/` before it disappears into chat**, even if we also implement it immediately.

**Do not write to Notion.** Do not use Notion MCP to create or update Tasks/Bugs for this repo. Hub source of truth is the Obsidian vault (`vault/`).

Read `.cursor/skills/obsidian-vault/SKILL.md` if the vault layout is unclear.

## Routing

| User intent | Destination | Defaults |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Feature / wishlist / "feat" | `vault/production/tasks/` | `type: task`, `task_type: Feature`, `status: Not started` |
| Bug / regression / broken behavior | `vault/production/bugs/` | `type: bug`, `status: Open`; fill Repro when known |

Templates: `vault/templates/task.md`, `vault/templates/bug.md`.

## How to write items

- **Title**: short, actionable (`feat:` / bug symptom), Russian or English OK — match surrounding board style. Filename = lowercase slug.
- **Area**: `Engine` | `Game` | `Production` when obvious; omit if unclear.
- **Body**: 2–5 lines — intent, acceptance hint, chat context. For bugs: steps / expected / actual.
- **Severity** (bugs): default `Medium` unless user implies Critical/High/Low.
- Assign `sprint` when the user schedules the item or when
  `link-followups-to-current-sprint.mdc` identifies it as follow-up work from
  the active sprint. Otherwise leave `sprint` empty.
- Deduplicate: Grep `vault/production/tasks/` and `vault/production/bugs/` first; if a close match exists, update that note instead of cloning.

## After create

- Reply with the **repo-relative path** and one-line title.
- Ask only if needed: implement now vs backlog.
- Pure clarifying questions and already-tracked sprint work do not need a new card.

## Exceptions (skip capture)

- Tiny implementation details inside an already open task ("rename this var").
- Explicit "не заводи задачу".
- Pure Q&A with no product ask.
